      <div type="translation" xml:lang="en"><p>The <title corresp="zh-a1" sameAs="摩訶般若波羅蜜經" type="sutra" ref="T_223" xml:id="en-a1">
                    <hi rend="italic">Great Perfection of Wisdom
                        Sutra</hi>
                </title> states: Emptiness of the Internal, Emptiness of the
                    External, Emptiness of both Internal and External, Emptiness of Emptiness, Great
                    Emptiness, Emptiness of the Primary Truth, Emptiness of the Conditioned,
                    Emptiness of the Unconditioned, Emptiness of the Ultimate, Emptiness of the
                    Beginningless, Emptiness of the Analyzed, Emptiness of Nature, Emptiness of <hi rend="italic">Dharmas</hi>,<ptr target="note_en_2"/> Emptiness of Self-<hi rend="italic">Dharmas</hi>,<ptr target="note_en_1"/> Emptiness of
                    Non-existent <hi rend="italic">Dharmas</hi>, Emptiness of Existent <hi rend="italic">Dharmas</hi>, Emptiness of <hi rend="italic">Dharmas</hi> that
                    are both Existent and Non-existent.</p></div>
